From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: add the Samsung S2MPB02 PMIC

The S2MPB02 is a Samsung companion PMIC for camera, display and sensor
rails: 18 LDOs, two bucks, a buck-boost and a flash/torch LED controller
behind one I2C address. The Galaxy Z Flip3 powers its cover panel's VCI
from LDO11 and its rear flash from the LED controller.

Document the PMIC node and its regulators. The flash LED sub-node is
documented with the LED binding.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpb02.yaml   | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 72 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpb02.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpb02.yaml
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpb02.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/mfd/samsung,s2mpb02.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Samsung S2MPB02 companion PMIC
+
+maintainers:
+  - Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
+
+description: |
+  The Samsung S2MPB02 is a companion power management IC for camera,
+  display and sensor rails in smart phones. It has 18 LDOs, two bucks, a
+  buck-boost converter and a flash/torch LED controller behind one I2C
+  address.
+
+  Only the regulators described under "regulators" are managed; the
+  others keep whatever state the bootloader left.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: samsung,s2mpb02
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  regulators:
+    type: object
+    description: The LDOs, bucks and the buck-boost.
+
+    patternProperties:
+      "^(ldo([1-9]|1[0-8])|buck[12]|bb)$":
+        type: object
+        $ref: /schemas/regulator/regulator.yaml#
+        unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+    additionalProperties: false
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        pmic@59 {
+            compatible = "samsung,s2mpb02";
+            reg = <0x59>;
+
+            regulators {
+                ldo11 {
+                    regulator-name = "panel_vci_sub";
+                    regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+                    regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+                    regulator-boot-on;
+                };
+
+                buck2 {
+                    regulator-name = "s2mpb02-b2";
+                    regulator-min-microvolt = <1300000>;
+                    regulator-max-microvolt = <1300000>;
+                    regulator-always-on;
+                };
+            };
+        };
+    };
